---
import Callout from "../../guide/Callout.astro";
import GuidePage from "../../guide/GuidePage.astro";
import Path from "../../guide/Path.astro";
import Task from "../../guide/Task.astro";
import WideShots from "../../guide/WideShots.astro";
import { plannedCapture } from "../../media/planned-captures.ts";
import { leavesSite, sitePath } from "../../site/links.ts";
---

<GuidePage manual="docs" slug="video" lead="Episodes play in Katari's built-in player, or in mpv once its add-on is installed. On Linux they play in mpv, which comes with Katari.">
  <Task id="player" title="Choose the player" platform="Android">
    <p>
      Every title starts on <strong>Auto</strong>, which uses the built-in player. If the <a href="#mpv-addon">mpv add-on</a> is
      installed, Auto switches to mpv for videos, audio or subtitles the built-in player can't handle, and goes back if mpv can't play
      them either.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>While an episode plays, tap the settings button at the top.</li>
      <li>Under <strong>Player</strong>, pick <strong>Auto</strong>, <strong>Built-in</strong> or <strong>mpv</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The choice applies to the whole title. On Auto, the same row says which player is in use and why.</p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="mpv-addon" title="The mpv add-on" platform="Android">
    <p>
      mpv plays formats and styled subtitles the built-in player can't. It is a separate app, downloaded from the
      <a href="https://github.com/pa2x2/mpv-android/releases" {...leavesSite()}>pa2x2/mpv-android releases</a>, and Katari only uses a
      copy signed with its own key.
    </p>
    <p>
      To install it, open <Path>Settings › Players › Anime player</Path> and tap <strong>Install</strong> beside
      <strong>mpv add-on</strong>. A video that needs mpv offers <strong>Install add-on</strong> as well. The delete button on the same
      row removes it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Katari keeps the add-on up to date along with itself. After an add-on update, tap <strong>Restart</strong> on its row; until then
      the old version keeps playing.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="mouse-and-keys" title="Mouse and keys" platform="Linux">
    <p>
      Click the picture to play or pause, double-click for full screen, and hold the button for 2× speed. Right-click opens the
      settings. The wheel sets the volume, scrolling sideways seeks, and Ctrl with the wheel or a touchpad pinch zooms. Ctrl with the
      arrow keys moves a zoomed picture.
    </p>
    <p>
      Space plays or pauses, the arrow keys seek and set the volume, F switches full screen, and I moves the episode to a small
      picture-in-picture window. Press ? to list every key. Hovering a button shows its key as well.
    </p>
    <WideShots
      shots={[
        { image: plannedCapture("desktop-keys.png"), alt: "The player listing every key it knows", caption: "Every key the player knows", device: "window" },
        {
          image: plannedCapture("desktop-pip.png"),
          alt: "An episode playing in the picture-in-picture window",
          caption: "Picture-in-picture",
          device: "picture-in-picture",
        },
      ]}
    />
  </Task>

  <Task id="servers" title="Pick a server, quality and tracks">
    <p>
      The player's settings button lists what the source and the video offer. <strong>Dub</strong>, <strong>Server</strong>,
      <strong>Stream</strong> and <strong>Source quality</strong> reload the episode, so they wait for <strong>Apply source</strong>.
      Quality, speed, audio and subtitles change at once.
    </p>
    <p>
      Katari remembers the dub, server and stream for each title. A title you haven't picked a quality for starts at
      <Path>Settings › Players › Anime player › Preferred quality</Path>.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a server fails while an episode loads, the player tells you and tries the next one. It never leaves a server you picked
      yourself; tap <strong>Try another server</strong> instead.
    </p>
    <WideShots
      shots={[
        {
          image: plannedCapture("player-settings.png"),
          alt: "The player's settings, with the server, quality and Apply source",
          caption: "The player's settings",
          device: "phone-landscape",
        },
      ]}
    />
  </Task>

  <Task id="skip" title="Skip intros and credits">
    <p>
      When the source marks intros, recaps, credits or previews, the timeline shows them and a skip button appears while they play. If
      only credits are left and another episode follows, the button says <strong>Next episode</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      When the source marks none, <Path>Settings › Players › Anime player › Find intro and credits times online</Path> looks them up
      on <strong>AniSkip</strong> and <strong>TheIntroDB</strong>, each with its own switch. Where both have times, AniSkip's are used.
    </p>
    <p>
      <Path>Settings › Players › Anime player › Skip intro and credits</Path> chooses between showing the button, skipping
      automatically, or neither. The player's settings have the same row for a single title. An automatic skip can be undone, and an
      intro that is part of the story is never skipped automatically.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task
    id="episodes"
    title="Filler, stills and summaries"
    shot={{ image: plannedCapture("episodes.png"), alt: "Episodes listed with their stills and a summary", caption: "Episodes with stills" }}
  >
    <p>
      Some sources mark filler episodes, and give episodes a still and a short summary. To hide filler, tap the filter button on the
      title's page and set <strong>Filler</strong> on the <strong>Filter</strong> tab. Continue and the player's next episode then skip
      it. Stills and summaries can be turned off with <strong>Previews and summaries</strong> on the <strong>Display</strong> tab.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="offline" title="Watch offline">
    <p>
      Downloading episodes opens a sheet where you choose the quality, and the dub, server, subtitles and audio when the source offers a
      choice. Subtitles start on the track the player would show; pick <strong>None</strong> to leave them out.
    </p>
    <p>Downloads resume after an interruption, keep their skip marks, and play in either player.</p>
    <Callout label="Can't be downloaded">
      <p>Live streams, copy-protected videos and episodes offered only as torrents.</p>
    </Callout>
  </Task>

  <Task id="extensions" title="Anime extensions">
    <p>
      Anime extensions made for Aniyomi work like any other. Add their store as in
      <a href={sitePath("docs/extension-stores/#add")}>Extension stores</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Katari doesn't play torrents. Extensions that only find torrents show as <strong>Torrents only</strong>. If a single episode is only
      offered as a torrent, pick another dub or server, or look for a streaming option in the source's settings.
    </p>
  </Task>
</GuidePage>
